{
  "slug": "vulca",
  "name": "Vulca",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Vulca adds agent-native visual workflows to Claude Code: visual discovery, brainstorm/spec/plan artifacts, structured prompt composition, semantic layer decomposition, and L1-L5 cultural evaluation. It is designed for reviewable image work instead of one-shot prompting, with local-first defaults and explicit opt-in for provider-backed generation, editing, and evaluation.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **7 skills**, **1 hook** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (7): `decompose` (Decompose an image into editable semantic layers using Vulca SDK), `evaluate` (Evaluate an existing visual artifact against a tradition, intent, and L1-L5 cultural/visual rubric), `using-vulca-skills` (Use when starting any conversation about Vulca visual workflows - establishes auto-invoke discipline for the discovery -> brainstorm…), `visual-brainstorm` (Use when the user wants to define a 2D illustrative or editorial visual project — poster, illustration, packaging,…), `visual-discovery` (Discover visual direction from fuzzy intent before /visual-brainstorm: taste profile, culture analysis, direction cards, and sketch prompts), `visual-plan` (Use when a design.md with status resolved already exists and you need to review plan.md then execute the…), `visual-spec` (Use when a proposal.md with status ready already exists and you need to derive a resolved design.md with…)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `vulca`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install vulca@claude-community` from `vulca-org/vulca-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 7,
    "hook": 1,
    "mcp": 1
  },
